      <title>Sale closed in San Jose: $2.4 million for a single-family home</title>
      <link>https://www.mercurynews.com/2026/02/24/sale-closed-in-san-jose-2-4-million-for-a-single-family-home-2/</link>
      <description>A 2,191-square-foot single-family home, built in 1963, has changed hands. The house in the 1600 block of Grizilo Drive in San Jose was sold on Jan. 15 for $2,410,000, or $1,100 per square foot. This two-story house has five bedrooms and three bathrooms. The interior features a fireplace. The property is equipped with a heating system. Additionally, the home includes access to a parking space for two cars. The lot of the property covers an area of 6,000 square feet.</description>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.mercurynews.com/2026/02/24/sale-closed-in-san-jose-2-4-million-for-a-single-family-home-2/</guid>
